ID:          6
Service:     service-c
Severity:    P1
Opened:      2026-05-29 16:29:26
Resolved:    2026-05-29 16:36:24
Title:       service-c degraded: health endpoint hardcoded to "degraded" (chaos mutation)
Report:      Root cause: uncommitted change in services/service-c/src/app.ts hardcoded { status: "degraded" } in the GET /health handler (was "ok"). service-c has no internal failure counter — its health is entirely determined by this literal value. The hardcoded degraded status caused the health-poller to permanently flag it as unhealthy. The POST /time handler was otherwise functional throughout.
Fix:         Restored const response: HealthResponse = { status: "ok" } in services/service-c/src/app.ts line 9.
QA:          Added regression test in services/service-c/src/__tests__/routes.test.ts: "returns status ok (not degraded) on a cold start — regression for hardcoded-degraded bug" — explicitly asserts GET /health does not return 503 or body { status: "degraded" } on a fresh app start.
