Title:       service-a /health hardcoded 503 + /time returns empty body
Report:      Health poller reported service-a degraded on every cycle. Root cause: services/service-a/src/app.ts:10 returned res.status(503) for GET /health even though the body was { status: "ok" }, so the poller always recorded degraded. Secondary defect: services/service-a/src/routes/time.ts built the TimeResponse but returned res.json({}) instead of res.json(response), so downstream service-b received utc=undefined and the b->a->c pipeline broke.
Fix:         services/service-a/src/app.ts: restored status-driven code res.status(response.status === "ok" ? 200 : 503). services/service-a/src/routes/time.ts: return res.json(response) instead of an empty object.
QA:          Existing service-a suite asserts GET /health -> 200 {status:"ok"} and GET /time -> body with a valid UTC ISO string; both pass against the fix (2/2). Full suite green.
