ID:          10
Service:     service-b
Severity:    P1
Opened:      2026-05-30 08:23:59
Resolved:    2026-05-30 08:30:19
Title:       service-b poll pipeline broken: FAILURE_THRESHOLD=0, wrong ports, bad timezone
Report:      Health poller reported service-b degraded on every cycle and no time_records were written after 08:17:51. Degraded health root cause: services/service-b/src/app.ts:7 set FAILURE_THRESHOLD=0, making consecutiveFailures >= 0 always true. Pipeline halt causes: SERVICE_A_URL and SERVICE_C_URL both pointed at port 3099 (ECONNREFUSED); timezone typo "America/New_Yrok" threw RangeError in Intl.DateTimeFormat on every poll. Recovery also required repairing service-c ingestion that service-b depends on: router mounted at /tiime instead of /time, handler declared GET instead of POST, and DB writes pointed at db/broken.db instead of db/sentinel.db.
Fix:         services/service-b/src/app.ts: FAILURE_THRESHOLD 0->3, SERVICE_A_URL ->http://localhost:3001, SERVICE_C_URL ->http://localhost:3003, timezone ->America/New_York. services/service-c/src/app.ts: mount router at /time. services/service-c/src/routes/time.ts: router.post("/") instead of get. services/service-c/src/db/index.ts: DB_PATH ->db/sentinel.db.
QA:          Added services/service-b regression test "stays ok after a poll with valid timezone conversion — regression for America/New_Yrok typo bug" (one successful poll keeps /health 200/ok, proving the tz conversion no longer throws). Added services/service-c/src/__tests__/db-path.test.ts "opens db/sentinel.db (not broken.db) — regression for wrong DB path bug" (mocks node:sqlite, asserts the opened path ends with db/sentinel.db). service-b 7/7 and service-c 5/5 pass.
